# Project Architecture Rules

## Tech Stack
- Next.js 15 App Router
- Supabase (no Prisma — raw SQL or Supabase JS client)
- TanStack Query (React Query v5) for data fetching/mutations
- TypeScript strict

---

## Folder Structure

src/
├── app/api/          # Next.js Route Handlers
│   └── [domain]/
│       ├── route.ts              # Entry point (GET, POST, PATCH, DELETE)
│       └── services/
│           └── actionName.ts     # One file per action, pure async logic
├── hooks/            # TanStack Query hooks (useQuery / useMutation)
├── models/           # TypeScript entity types (mirrors Supabase tables)
├── constants/
│   └── apiRouter.ts  # All API route strings centralized here
└── types/
    └── response.type.ts

---

## Rule 1 — API Route Handler (route.ts)

- Location: `src/app/api/[domain]/[resource]/route.ts`
- Only handles HTTP plumbing: parse params/body, call service, return NextResponse
- No business logic inside route.ts
- Always await `context.params` (Next.js 15 dynamic params are Promises)
- Return `NextResponse.json(result, { status: result.status ?? 500 })`

### Template:
\`\`\`typescript
import { NextResponse } from 'next/server'
import { someService } from './services/someService'

type RouteContext = { params: Promise<{ id: string }> }

export async function GET(_request: Request, context: RouteContext) {
  const { id } = await context.params
  const result = await someService(id)
  return NextResponse.json(result, { status: result.status ?? 500 })
}

export async function PATCH(request: Request, context: RouteContext) {
  const { id } = await context.params
  try {
    const body = await request.json()
    const result = await someService(id, body)
    if (!result.ok) return NextResponse.json({ error: result.error }, { status: 400 })
    return NextResponse.json({ ok: true })
  } catch {
    return NextResponse.json({ error: 'Invalid body' }, { status: 400 })
  }
}
\`\`\`

---

## Rule 2 — Service Files

- Location: `src/app/api/[domain]/[resource]/services/actionName.ts`
- One file = one action (e.g. `getOrderDetail.ts`, `updateOrderStatus.ts`)
- Returns a typed result object, never throws to route
- Use Supabase JS client directly here
- Export the DTO type if needed (used by hooks)

### Return convention:
\`\`\`typescript
// Success
return { ok: true, data: ..., status: 200 }

// Error
return { ok: false, error: 'message', status: 400 }
\`\`\`

### Template:
\`\`\`typescript
import { createClient } from '@/lib/supabase/server'

export type CreateXxxDTO = {
  field: string
}

export async function createXxx(dto: CreateXxxDTO) {
  const supabase = await createClient()
  const { data, error } = await supabase.from('table').insert(dto).select().single()
  if (error) return { ok: false, error: error.message, status: 500 }
  return { ok: true, data, status: 201 }
}
\`\`\`

---

## Rule 3 — Models (Entity Types)

- Location: `src/models/entityName.ts`
- Mirrors Supabase table columns exactly (snake_case)
- No class, only `type`
- Nullable columns → `field: Type | null`
- Define status union types in same file
- Extended/joined types use `& {}` pattern

### Template:
\`\`\`typescript
/**
 * Xxx entity (table: xxx)
 */
export type XxxStatus = 'active' | 'inactive'

export type Xxx = {
  id: string
  name: string | null
  status: XxxStatus | null
  created_at: Date | null
  updated_at: Date | null
}

export type XxxWithRelation = Xxx & {
  relation?: RelationType | null
}
\`\`\`

---

## Rule 4 — TanStack Query Hooks

- Location: `src/hooks/useXxx.ts`
- Must have `'use client'` at top
- Fetch function defined above the hook (not inside)
- Query key convention: `['@scope-resource', ...params]`
- Use `placeholderData: (prev) => prev` for paginated queries
- Toast on mutation success/error via `sonner`
- Invalidate related queries on mutation success

### useQuery template:
\`\`\`typescript
'use client'
import { useQuery } from '@tanstack/react-query'
import { API_ROUTES } from '@/constants/apiRouter'

async function fetchXxx(id: string) {
  const res = await fetch(API_ROUTES.XXX.GET(id), { cache: 'no-store' })
  if (!res.ok) throw new Error('Fetch failed')
  return res.json()
}

export function useXxx(id: string) {
  return useQuery({
    queryKey: ['@xxx', id],
    queryFn: () => fetchXxx(id),
  })
}
\`\`\`

### useMutation template:
\`\`\`typescript
'use client'
import { useMutation, useQueryClient } from '@tanstack/react-query'
import { API_ROUTES } from '@/constants/apiRouter'
import { toast } from 'sonner'

export function useUpdateXxx() {
  const qc = useQueryClient()
  return useMutation({
    mutationFn: async (payload: { id: string; field: string }) => {
      const res = await fetch(API_ROUTES.XXX.PATCH(payload.id), {
        method: 'PATCH',
        headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
        body: JSON.stringify(payload),
      })
      const data = await res.json().catch(() => ({}))
      if (!res.ok) throw new Error(data?.error || 'Thất bại')
      return data
    },
    onSuccess: () => {
      void qc.invalidateQueries({ queryKey: ['@xxx'] })
      toast.success('Cập nhật thành công')
    },
    onError: (e: Error) => {
      toast.error(e.message || 'Có lỗi xảy ra')
    },
  })
}
\`\`\`

---

## Rule 5 — API Routes Constants

- All API URLs must be defined in `src/constants/apiRouter.ts`
- Never hardcode URL strings in hooks or components

\`\`\`typescript
export const API_ROUTES = {
  XXX: {
    GET_ALL: '/api/admin/xxx',
    GET: (id: string) => `/api/admin/xxx/${id}`,
    PATCH: (id: string) => `/api/admin/xxx/${id}`,
    DELETE: (id: string) => `/api/admin/xxx/${id}`,
  },
}
\`\`\`

---

## General Rules

- No `any` type — always type properly or use `unknown`
- Prefer `type` over `interface`
- snake_case for DB columns, camelCase for JS variables
- Always handle Supabase error object: `if (error) return { ok: false, error: error.message }`
- No business logic in route.ts or hooks — logic belongs in services
- Keep each file focused: one responsibility per file